    holmgard: 'Two roads run out of the north country, and this is where they part. The south road runs to the Greek sea and Miklagard. The east road runs to the Volga: the Msta corridor and its haul-overs, the timber waypoint at Timerevo, the great market at Bulgar, the khagan\u2019s city at Itil \u2014 and past the delta, by caravan, Baghdad, the City of Peace, a road no keel sails whole. One season, either way. The east is the farther reach, and they say the furs pay for the distance.',
